  "whyItMatters": "The same magnitude along another axis is a different load case: gravity applied horizontally becomes a sway load, a load along the member axis produces axial force instead of bending, and a load out of the plane of a plane frame goes straight into the out-of-plane restraints or bends the members about their weak axis. With Y-up and Z-up conventions both in use this is an easy slip.",
